will be expelled. Fifth, the receiving of the four empowerments: by making such a prayer, the Master <term>Heruka</term> and so forth are invoked. Through their union, a stream of nectar descends from their heart-life-force. From the point of their union, it comes down in the form of white and red <term>bodhichitta</term>. It passes through one's own <term>dhuti</term>, filling the inside of the body. This purifies the conceptual obscurations such as attachment and the fixation on the ordinary body. The knots of the channels are untied, and the vase empowerment is obtained. One is empowered to meditate on the generation stage of the body as the deity’s body, like an illusion. Again, the stream of nectar descends. The general stains of ordinary speech, and especially all the afflictions arising from hatred, are purified. The wind enters the <term>dhuti</term>, and the secret empowerment is obtained. One is empowered to recite the speech mantras or to meditate on the two aspects of the illusory body. The nectar, as before—
